<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39126" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōtēlum</span></b> , i,
			n.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A row of oxen</i>, etc., <i>harnessed
				together for draught</i>, <i>a team</i>: protelo
			trini boves unum aratrum ducent, Cato ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. 363, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lucil.
				ib. 363, 7</span></i> and 8: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">boum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 15, 17, § 45</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bina ternaque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					18, 18, 48, § 173</span></i>
			; cf.: protelum, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔξαμπρον</span>,
			Gloss. Philox.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a line</i>, <i>row</i>, <i>succession</i>
			(ante-class. and <b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">protelo plagarum continuato,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 531</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4,
		190</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
